WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.526
Map data from its source to every processor, queue, cache, log, and backup.

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:15.303
Label trust boundaries where information moves between user devices, local servers, gateways, cloud accounts, providers, and third-party APIs.

00:00:15.303 --> 00:00:22.279
For each crossing, record the data class, purpose, recipient, encryption, retention, and authorized identities.

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:27.455
A diagram is valuable only when it reflects runtime behavior.

00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:36.681
Prompt filtering can block prohibited fields, detect secrets, or redact identifiers before external use, but it is not infallible.

00:00:36.681 --> 00:00:43.207
Documents may reveal sensitive information through retrieved passages, filenames, embedded metadata, or summaries.

00:00:43.207 --> 00:00:50.184
Test filters against realistic inputs and define a safe action when classification is uncertain.

00:00:50.184 --> 00:00:54.909
Some data should never enter an automatic cloud route.

00:00:54.909 --> 00:00:59.635
Logs deserve the same classification as prompts and outputs.

00:00:59.635 --> 00:01:09.312
Gateways, model servers, tracing tools, application telemetry, and provider consoles may record content, tokens, account identifiers, errors, and tool calls.

00:01:09.312 --> 00:01:15.838
Minimize content logging, restrict access, encrypt transport and storage, and set retention intentionally.

00:01:15.838 --> 00:01:23.714
Confirm provider data-use and deletion terms rather than assuming an API request disappears after the response.

00:01:23.714 --> 00:01:30.240
Enforce policy close to the routing decision and again at destination access controls.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.317
Maintain evidence of which route processed a request without retaining unnecessary content.

00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:42.393
Review data flows when a model, provider, plugin, or observability tool changes.

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:51.169
Hybrid privacy depends on controlling copies and metadata throughout the path, not merely keeping the original document local.
